{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551490-black-wind-demon-arts","id":1551490,"title":"Black Wind (Demon Arts)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-05T20:16:30-07:00","id":1551490,"title":"Black Wind (Demon Arts)","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused with the usage of the Black Wind, bolding the relevant parts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Wind p.107 Kindred of the East Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allowing the rage of the P'o to channel itself through her<br /> body, the Kuei-jin becomes inhumanly swift \u2014 a typhoon of<br /> destruction. Essentially, Black Wind is a focused \u2014 or not so<br /> focused\u2014frenzy. While in the Black Wind state, the character<br /> gains powers similar to prolonged use of Demon Chi (see p. 91),<br /> but<b> because the character is in a continuous demonic fury, she<br /> gains demonic energy as fast as she uses it. </b>This Discipline is a<br /> common one among more warlike Kuei-jin, who use it to<br /> become whirling blurs of carnage.<br /> System: <b>This power costs the Kuei-jin one point of Demon<br /> Chi per turn of use.<br /> ...</b><br /> <b>Moreover, each turn the power is<br /> used, the vampire must roll P'o (difficulty 8); if he fails this roll, he<br /> enters fire soul. </b>A frenzied vampire suffers no wound penalties, but<br /> may not use firearms or any other missile weapons; he instead<br /> prefers to shred foes face to face \u2014 of course, such is the intent of<br /> most who use Black Wind.<b> The problem lies in the fact that a<br /> vampire using this power just as readily attacks allies as enemies.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>My questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Using Black Wind is essentially costless after the starting point? It seems to be regenerating as much as it is being spent.</li> <li>There is no time limit except by how long the P'o roll can succeed?</li> <li>Is the P'o roll JUST the P'o?</li> <li>If the roll is failed, is the vampire still under the effects of the Black Wind? If so, when will the effect stop? After leaving Fire Soul?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-06-2025, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-06T00:56:55-07:00","id":1551495,"title":"","content":"1 - it is not. The writing for this Discipline is just confusing - seemingly, on purpose.<br /> 2 - It's for every turn you use BW. Also, see below for an extra helping of urine in your cereal grains.<br /> 3 - Yes. Though, according to Vrev ST Handbook, you actually have to make two rolls when you want to use BW - Hun (diff Po) and Po (diff 8).<br /> 4 - I'm going to give you the Abridged Mr. Satan answer.<br /> <br /> &quot;That things broken, right?&quot;<br /> &quot;FUBAR, sir.&quot;<br /> &quot;I got no fuckin' idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can only say that KotE and BW in particular were subject to the most onerous backtracking and fearful sense of &quot;holy shit what did we do?&quot; out of everything in Vampire. Bringing back the Salubri and also detailing Gui Ren using Dragon's Tear to rip souls out of people? No problemo. Having an on the edge Discipline that gives characters an advantage in combat somewhat comparable to Celerity or Rage, but with some extra versatility? BACK THE FUCK UP!<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, highly hypocritical in light of how Celerity was always the most godawfully busted and broken Disciplines ever until V20. Possibly even after it, too. And also how BW is twice the cost of in-Clan Celerity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}